"poll_weight": 0.29, "fundamentals": {"margin": -0.09, "lean": -7.0, "environment": 8.1, "incumbency": 0.0, "money": -1.19}, "rating_margin": -9.67, "sigma_race": 6.0, "sigma_total": 6.84, "baseline_margin": -4.53, "analyst_adjustment": 0.53, "key_factors": ["District's R+7 partisan lean in a favorable Democratic national environment", "Open seat with Republican nominee Flippo lacking Amodei's endorsement after a divisive primary", "Recent polls show a near-tied race, though samples are small and partly Dem-sponsored", "Most expert raters still call the race Likely R"], "rationale": "The seat's Republican lean and the Likely R consensus keep the GOP favored, but the open seat, Amodei's rift with Flippo, and polling showing a one-to-three point contest justify moving well inside the lean. Fundraising is lopsided toward Flippo, yet outside money and ratings cap Democratic upside.", "watch": "A late round of independent-quality polling or a major Flippo scandal could tip this into tossup territory.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Mark Amodei (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Mark Amodei's retirement leaves this Reno-area seat open for the first time in years, and the race is closer than usual for a district that leans Republican by about seven points. Democrat Teresa Benitez-Thompson faces Republican David Flippo, who won a contentious primary with Trump's backing but has drawn an ethics-related inquiry and lacks Amodei's support. Recent polls show a narrow contest, though samples are small and some are sponsored by Democratic groups.\n\nMost forecasters still rate the seat Likely or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give the Democrat roughly a one-in-five chance. Flippo's large fundraising edge and the district's fundamentals keep him favored, but the open-seat dynamics and a favorable national environment for Democrats make this more competitive than a typical cycle here.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.213, "margin": -